# admin-ui environment variables (Vite reads these at build/dev time).
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and uncomment to override. Any file matching
# `.env*` other than this example is gitignored, so local overrides stay local.

# Base URL the REST client prefixes onto every request.
#
# Leave UNSET for local development: the client defaults to `/api`, which the
# Vite dev proxy (see vite.config.ts) forwards to the backend on
# http://localhost:8080. This is the same-origin, no-CORS path.
#
# Set to a full origin to point the (dev or built) app straight at a backend,
# e.g. when serving the production build against a remote gsy-offchain-storage.
# That backend must allow this origin (CORS); the UI does not add CORS itself.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://some-host:8080
